WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:05.190 align:start position:0%
 
it's  t for one for prince william the duke of  cambridge is carrying on with his royal  duties as his wife  kate middleton continues to self-isolate  following an exposure to covid19  the 39 year old royal hosted the big t  event  on monday solo at buckingham palace  honoring national health service staff  and frontline workers  the occasion the 73rd anniversary of the  nhs england's national health service  and the party was originally supposed to  include  kate but it was announced on sunday that  the mom of three was self-isolating at  home  after coming into contact with someone  who tested positive for covid19  a royal source previously confirmed to  et that the duchess received  both of her vaccinations after going  public with the first one  in late may prior to the news of her  exposure  kate was all smiles as she attended  wimbledon on friday  toured the museum and helped out in the  community kitchen  but despite his wife's absence william  carried out the event  and praised the healthcare heroes for  their tireless work  video of the outdoor gathering was  shared on the cambridge's official  instagram account  earlier in the day the 39 year old royal  attended the service of thanksgiving at  saint paul's cathedral in london  in honor of the special occasion the  queen awarded the george cross award to  the  nhs sharing this handwritten letter on  social media which read in part  quote over more than seven decades and  especially in recent times  you have supported the people of our  country with courage  compassion and dedication demonstrating  the highest stands of public service  you have our enduring thanks and  heartfelt appreciation  the george cross is awarded for acts of  heroism in circumstances of extreme  danger  and it's the uk's highest award for  non-military courage  meanwhile william's brother prince harry  has returned home to california from the  uk  after reuniting with his brother for the  unveiling of the princess diana statue  in honor of what would have been their  late mother's 60th birthday  of course the reunion was a big deal as  it came amid reports that the two  brothers are at  odds following harry's decision to step  back from his senior royal duties in  2020  and his explosive tell-all interview  with oprah winfrey earlier this year  there's clearly still a lot of hurt a  lot of resentment  and a degree of mistrust i think on both  parts  but i think the hope is that come july  when we are hoping to see the brothers  stand once again shoulder by shoulders  that the relationship will be  stronger and in a better place the  statue unveiling marked the first time  the brothers had publicly come  face to face since april when they  attended the funeral of their  grandfather prince philip  diana always said to them always stay  close  don't ever fall out she would be  devastated that that is what happened  and she would be wanting them to feed  her together for that unveiling of the  statue in her honor  et spoke to royal expert katie nichol  after the brothers reunited  she weighed in on the significance of  the day of course as much  as everyone wanted to see what the  statue looked like  all eyes were on william and harry and  their body chemistry  and how they were interacting with each  other so as they  arrived at the sunken garden at  kensington palace they were walking  side by side and they were engaged in a  conversation  i watched it and thought how comfortable  they looked in each other's company  there wasn't any sign of  of any tension now i think both of them  have wanted today to be about the statue  about remembering diana's legacy and not  about the rift that has really  overshadowed the coverage  of the royal family for the past 18  months now so  they clearly went to a lot of effort to  deflect from this rift  between the two of them and instead to  project on  their mother a legacy and crucially  putting on a united front to remember  diana  their mother on what would have been her  60th birthday  you

